<title>FRANCE: FRENCH ELECTION - LATEST OPINION POLLS.</title>
<headline>FRENCH ELECTION - LATEST OPINION POLLS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of opinion polls conducted since President Jacques Chirac dissolved the National Assembly on April 21 and called a snap election for May 25 and June 1.</p>
<p>The dates indicate when the poll was taken. The first table is of voting intentions in percentage terms. Most surveys have a margin of error of plus or minus two percent.</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Polling institute	    CSA	Ipsos</p>
<p>				 April 22  April 22-23</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		    1	   1.5</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists			9	  10</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left	28	  29</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Ecologists			6	   5</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR-UDF-other right	  43	  39.5</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front		 13	  15</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The second table, with a wider margin of error, is of projections in seats in the 577-seat Assembly. Where polling institutes give a range, the figure used is the median point of the spread.</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Polling institute	    CSA*     Ipsos</p>
<p>				 April 22   April 22-23</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> extreme left		   0	    0</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		    20	   28</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left    201	  256</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> ecologists		     1	    0</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR-UDF-other right	332	  292</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front		 1	    1</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>*poll only covers the 555 constituencies in metropolitan France, not the 22 seats in overseas departments and territories, most of which were held by the centre-right coalition in the outgoing Assembly.</p>
</text>
